 node.innerHTML=`<div class="eyebrow">TESTING THE NEXT VERSION</div><h2>Three views of this matchup</h2><p>The expanded model uses ${upgradeData.trainingGames.toLocaleString()} past games. These comparison forecasts help us evaluate the next version.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Projected score</th><th>Home win chance</th></tr></thead><tbody>${rows.map(([label,p])=>`<tr><td>${esc(label)}</td><td>${esc(upgradeScore(p,g))}</td><td>${p?pct(p.p):'Unavailable'}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="tiny">The odds version uses ${Math.round(r.marketWeight*100)}% sportsbook weight for the winning margin. Its total comes from the history model. Probabilities are model estimates, including the odds version. Injury adjustments have not been fitted. All scores use a one-point rounding tiebreak when needed.</p><details class="technical"><summary>Forecast timing and missing information</summary><p>Saved ${esc(new Date(upgradeData.generatedAt).toLocaleString('en-US',{timeZone:'America/New_York'}))} ET using game results through ${esc(upgradeData.asOf)}. Odds snapshot: ${esc(r.marketSnapshot.retrievedAt?new Date(r.marketSnapshot.retrievedAt).toLocaleString('en-US',{timeZone:'America/New_York'})+' ET':'unavailable')}. These are saved forecasts and do not refresh automatically.</p><p>Verified player availability, replacement experience and historical line injuries still need a consistent dataset before we can learn their effects. The matchup’s injury watch provides the reports currently available.</p></details>`;
}
