 return `<article id="upgradeResults"><div class="eyebrow">NEW MODEL TEST</div><h2>More history. Measured results.</h2><p>The expanded model now trains on <b>${u.trainingGames.toLocaleString()} games</b>. Here is how it compares on the same ${next.n} games used in our original test.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Winner accuracy</th><th>Average margin error</th><th>Upset picks</th></tr></thead><tbody>${performance('Current model',old)}${performance('Expanded history',next)}</tbody></table></div><p>${n>0?`${n} more correct winners`:n<0?`${-n} fewer correct winners`:'The same number of correct winners'}. ${next.marginMAE>old.marginMAE?'Winning margins were less accurate, so the current model continues to provide the main picks.':'The full comparison is still experimental; saved future forecasts will provide the next check.'}</p><details class="technical"><summary>Did adding sportsbook odds help?</summary><p>We tested five weights: 0%, 25%, 50%, 75% and 100% sportsbook influence on the winning margin. The first ${b.earlier.n} games selected <b>${Math.round(b.weight*100)}%</b>. On the next ${b.later.n} games, that version picked <b>${b.later.wins} winners correctly (${upgradePct(b.later.accuracy)})</b>.</p><p>${b.weight===1?'The selected version followed the sportsbook line entirely. Our added football features did not improve the earlier-period margin predictions over the line alone.':'The selected version combined the line with our history model.'}</p><p>These use final pregame lines retrieved afterward. They may include news unavailable when an earlier prediction would have been made. This experiment does not establish a live betting advantage.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Sportsbook weight</th><th>First ${b.earlier.n}: margin error</th><th>Next ${b.later.n}: winner accuracy</th><th>Next ${b.later.n}: margin error</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.values(u.blends).map(r=>`<tr><td>${Math.round(r.weight*100)}%</td><td>${r.earlier.marginMAE.toFixed(1)}</td><td>${upgradePct(r.later.accuracy)} · ${r.later.wins}/${r.later.n}</td><td>${r.later.marginMAE.toFixed(1)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div></details><details class="technical"><summary>Season tests and score accuracy</summary><p>We chose between two fixed versions using 2024 results, then evaluated 2025 separately. Each season’s model was fitted on earlier seasons; team statistics update only after earlier game dates. These are historical replays.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th>Games</th><th>Correct winners</th><th>Margin error</th></tr></thead><tbody>${Object.entries(u.seasonResults[u.selected]).map(([year,r])=>`<tr><td>${year}${year==='2026'?' through Oct 20':''}</td><td>${r.n}</td><td>${upgradePct(r.accuracy)}</td><td>${r.marginMAE.toFixed(1)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>These full-season groups contain different matchups from the original ${next.n}-game test. Their percentages cannot be compared directly with its ${upgradePct(old.accuracy)} result.</p><p>On the same ${next.n} games, combined-score error was ${old.totalMAE.toFixed(1)} points for the current model and ${next.totalMAE.toFixed(1)} for expanded history. The expanded model caught ${next.upsetWins} of ${next.actualUpsets} actual upsets, compared with ${old.upsetWins} for the current model.</p><p>${esc(u.protocol.coverage)}</p></details><details class="technical"><summary>Injuries and matchup combinations</summary><p>Center and line evidence currently covers ${u.availability.verifiedTeams} teams. We still need historical, dated availability records to estimate player effects. Reports alone cannot tell us how many points a replacement costs.</p><p>The next combinations to test are replacement center + QB road experience + pass rush; missing tackles + edge pressure; and missing interior defenders + rushing strength. No numerical injury effect has been fitted.</p></details><p class="tiny">${u.forecasts.length